	abstract = {The field of soft robotics has emerged as a transformative technology in the medical and healthcare industries. This chapter provides a comprehensive study on the materials used in soft robotics, focusing on their properties, applications, and the advantages they offer in medical contexts. We explore a range of materials, including silicone elastomers, hydrogels, shape-memory alloys, and electroactive polymers, detailing how each contributes to the functionality and adaptability of soft robotic systems. Special emphasis is placed on biocompatibility, mechanical flexibility, and environmental responsiveness that enhance the performance of soft robots in applications such as surgical assistance, rehabilitation devices, and prosthetics. Through case studies and examples, we illustrate the innovative uses of these materials in real-world healthcare scenarios, highlighting their impact on patient outcomes and the future potential of soft robotics in medicine. This chapter aims to provide researchers and practitioners with a thorough understanding of material selection in soft robotics, facilitating advancements in the design and application of these promising technologies in the healthcare sector. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Shaik Himam Saheb, Tharakeshwar Appala and Mohammad S Khan.},
